    <string name="privacy">Privacy</string>
    <string name="privacy_body">Cycle data stays in app-private storage. Selia Cycles has no account, ads, analytics, app cloud, or network permission. If you enable calendar sync, only short cycle labels are copied to the calendar you choose; its provider controls any account upload.</string>
    <string name="about_cycle">How the menstrual cycle works</string>
    <string name="cycle_info_body">A cycle starts on the first day of bleeding and ends the day before the next period. Hormones prepare the uterus for pregnancy. If pregnancy does not occur, the uterine lining is shed as menstrual bleeding. Adult cycles often vary; 24–38 days is a common clinical range, and bleeding often lasts about 2–7 days. Ovulation timing varies, so calendar estimates cannot confirm ovulation and must not be used as contraception. Seek healthcare advice for very heavy bleeding, severe pain, bleeding between periods, or a marked change in your usual pattern.</string>
